Require a separately verified untouched matching vendor-module baseline
before applying this patch to a new output copy. Generation is not build,
application, module loading, hardware execution or a successful repair.

The new bool defaults false/0400. Only an explicit module option together
with /chosen/linux,booted-from-kexec and the exact qcom,sun-gcc device enables
the experiment. Immediately before the existing clock registration call,
OR the existing FORCE_ENABLE_RCG flag into gcc_ufs_phy_phy_aux_clk_src.flags
and log the old/new software flags. No other clock is changed. Keep the
existing HW_CLK_CTRL_MODE, safe configuration, rate and parent definitions.

The unchanged actual clk_rcg2_ops provider then retains ROOT_EN during its
normal enable lifecycle; its original disable still parks at CXO and clears
force. There are no new MMIO accesses, retries or resets in this patch, and
no error-handling bypass. Original provider return-value limitations remain:
force-enable polling may warn and return zero, and configure errors may leave
the force bit set. A zero callback return is not hardware-on proof. Inspect
actual clock status and the original leaf/PHY/UFS errors during a bounded
reversible boot experiment. This is not a production power-management fix.

